  "equipment_type": "Boiler and water heater plant controller via ProtoNode gateway",
  "applies_to": "AERCO C-More boilers running on-board BST sequencing and C-More water heaters (KC, Innovation) running WHM, up to 8 units, through the ProtoNode RER SSD profile.",
  "summary": "With the SSD (Slave/Slave Device) profile the AERCO ProtoNode RER sits on the BST or WHM Modbus network at fixed address 247 and serves the master's operating values and a 20-value block for each of up to 8 units on BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP. The BMS changes the plant setpoint and setback values by writing them and then writing 1 to a send command. This file lists the master points and unit 1.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "Node_Offset + A-bank DIP switch value (MAC); the manual's example uses Node_Offset 50,000",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Older document (OMM-0080_0H, November 2014) for the ProtoNode RER gateway.",
    "Unit blocks: unit n (1-8) uses AV 200 + 100 x n to AV 219 + 100 x n, so unit 1 = AV 300-319 and unit 8 = AV 1000-1019; only unit 1 is listed here.",
    "Run cycles = upper x 65536 + lower; run hours the same.",
    "Setback times are minutes after midnight (360 = 6 AM).",
    "The SSD keeps fixed Modbus address 247 so communication resumes after a BST/WHM master failover without BAS changes.",
    "The manual's point name for AV 313 is spelled Value State; the definition table calls it Valve State."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Select the SSD BACnet profile on the ProtoNode (S1 and A3 On, all other S and A1 Off); the gateway then talks to the BST/WHM master at address 247. To change the plant setpoint write AV 200 (and setback values AV 201-203 if used), then write 1 to AV 51 to send them. Read plant values from AV 100-119 and each unit's block from AV 300 onwards.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 200",
        "name": "Setpt",
        "why": "Plant setpoint to send, 40-200 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 51",
        "name": "Write Cntrl Val to BST/WHM",
        "why": "Write 1 to send AV 200-203 to the master"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 107",
        "name": "Units Active",
        "why": "Units active, 0-8"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 301",
        "name": "Unit Status",
        "why": "Unit 1 status; 5 = Fault"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 101",
        "name": "Setpoint",
        "why": "Plant setpoint in use, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 110",
        "name": "Header Temp",
        "why": "Header temperature, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 106",
        "name": "Avg Outlet Temp",
        "why": "Average outlet temperature, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 108",
        "name": "Units Faulted",
        "why": "Number of faulted units, 0-8"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 302",
        "name": "Fault Code",
        "why": "Unit 1 fault code (C-More codes)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No start/stop object. Write the new setpoint (AV 200) and, if used, setback setpoint and times (AV 201-203), then write 1 to AV 51 Write Cntrl Val to BST/WHM to pass them to the master.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "SSD BACnet profile: S1 On and A3 On, S0/S2/S3 and A1 Off (SSD Modbus and SSD N2 profiles also exist).",
      "Device instance = Node_Offset (set in the Web Configurator) + A-bank DIP value; MS/TP MAC is 1-127 on A0-A7, baud on B0-B3.",
      "Default IP 192.168.1.24; change it in the ProtoNode web GUI.",
      "Modbus side: every AERCO unit at 9600 baud, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no parity.",
      "The gateway uses SSD address 247 on the BST/WHM Modbus network; units keep their own addresses."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Writes to AV 200-203 do nothing until 1 is written to AV 51.",
      "AV 53 is read only despite sitting with the control values: 0 = WHM present, 1 = WHM absent.",
      "Unit Type codes 6-8 (water heaters) apply to WHM only; BST uses 1-5."
    ]
  },
